# Embedded templates are compiled into the `aida` binary by build.rs; pin
# them to LF so a Windows checkout (git autocrlf) cannot embed CRLF, which
# would otherwise break frontmatter parsing of the starter memory pack.
# Defense-in-depth — the load-bearing fix is parser-side line-ending
# normalization (normalize_line_endings). trace:BUG-244
aida-core/templates/** text eol=lf

# Keep the checked-in project copy under the same contract as the embedded
# master. The comparison also normalizes defensively, but this prevents a
# Windows checkout from manufacturing drift on disk. trace:BUG-1555 | ai:codex
.aida/discipline/** text eol=lf

# Rust sources: pin to LF so a Windows autocrlf checkout cannot hand
# `include_str!` source-shape tests CRLF text (their `\n}\n` body-end
# searches then silently span the whole file). The tests also normalise
# defensively. trace:BUG-1556 | ai:claude
*.rs text eol=lf
